              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Keywords" typeId="d6ab-192f-515b-f06b">USA, (CORE) Mechanized, (CORE) Starborne, Attache (Troop), Hero, Command</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Base Size" typeId="7451-1f52-67d5-01a8">32mm</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Maximum Number in Platoon" typeId="d3f4-a3f4-2fe1-5fee">1</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Filthy Thirteen" id="dc26-7e3f-e0a1-1827" hidden="false">
              <description>Before the Game begins, if the total number of models in this Platoon is equal to 13, all of them gain the following bonuses:
* Demolition Section: This Unit may perform the Demolish Action as a Standard Action
* Explosive Priorities: If this Unit is within 3&quot; of an Objective, it may, as a Standard Action, Set Charges. If it does, a Charge is set on that Objective. When that Charge is Detonated, all Units within 3&quot; are Attacked by the Satchel Charge Profile, and the Objective is removed from the Battlefield. 
* Friendly Units within 8&quot; of a Charge may, as an Action, attempt to Detonate it. If they do, roll 1D10, on a 9+, the Charge is Detonated.
* Enemy Units within 3&quot; of a Charge may, as an Action, attempt to Defuse it. If they do, roll 1D10, on a 9+, the Charge is removed.
* Each failed attempt to Detonate or Defuse grants a stacking +1 to their respective checks.
* Each time you successfully Detonate the Charges, you gain VP equal to the per-round value of the Objective destroyed.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Rebellious" id="39ce-1b1f-21f1-2fcd" hidden="false">
              <description>First Sergeant Jake McNiece may not be your Field Commander. 

First Sergeant Jake McNiece may only be taken if your selected Army Specialization is US Army 101st Airborne Division “Screaming Eagles”</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
