    <selectionEntryGroup name="Army Specializations" id="67a5-9279-11b3-fbad" hidden="false">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="36de-1770-d02c-1d56" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="US Army 1st Infantry Division “Big Red One”" id="e3f5-e2b1-bd65-31d6" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="1" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Red Ball Express" id="778f-b2b7-589e-e667" hidden="false">
              <description>During Deployment, after all Units have been deployed, place a Supply Depot Tent (represented by the Command Tent Terrain Feature) anywhere wholly within your Deployment Zone without spending Supply Points or Actions to deploy.

*This does not count as a deployed model for the purposes of deciding who goes first.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Expanding Supply Lines" id="cd55-eb64-23cc-7acf" hidden="false">
              <description>Any time during a Unit’s activation, if it is within 8” of a friendly fortification with the Supply Line keyword, you may spend Supply Points to perform a free action from the Supply Line Action Table. A Unit may only perform one of these Free Actions per Round. Each time a Supply Line Action is used, its cost increases by 1SP until the end of the Round.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Supply Line Actions Reference" id="ec36-4768-a793-f7b7" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="6abd-484e-5b29-633c" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="1: Get to Digging: 0 SP" id="1423-789e-8aef-bceb" hidden="false">
                  <description>If this unit has the Troop Keyword, perform the Build Action as a free action.                


 *They do not need to have Build in their list of available actions.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="3: Back in Action: 2 SP" id="531d-3c9f-2fd4-fb24" hidden="false">
                  <description>This unit regains 4 HP or 4 HP worth of destroyed models.         
*This can only revive models if the amount of HP is equal to their starting health or less.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="2: Go Rolling Along: 1 SP" id="6bc7-5882-214d-d873" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Unit is issued an Order.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="4: Locked and Loaded: 2 SP" id="0906-31e3-cd2b-a71a" hidden="false">
                  <description>Reload a weapon this unit is equipped with that has the Ammo Special Rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="5: Target in Sight: 2 SP" id="72b2-52ea-abc5-c733" hidden="false">
                  <description>Tick the Dial In counter by 1.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="6: The Full Nine Yards: 6 SP" id="f5d0-9693-2a52-c3b6" hidden="false">
                  <description>Select one weapon profile of this unit, perform an additional Attack Action with that weapon as a free action.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="US Army 101st Airborne Division “Screaming Eagles”" id="42e5-eb30-4d39-61a3" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="2" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Screaming Eagles" id="cbef-1a3a-4543-dff0" hidden="false">
              <description>At the start of the first Setup phase, you may select any number of non-transport Units with the Troop or Light Keywords to gain the Air Assault Special Rule. At least 50% of your Army must be deployed with the Air Assault Special Rule.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Rendezvous With Destiny" id="9cfd-22fe-75d9-aeb3" hidden="false">
              <description>Airstrike Special Requistions cost 1 fewer I.P.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Currahee!" id="f832-557e-28a6-caab" hidden="false">
              <description>Units in your army that have the Flying keyword, or are at least one level above targeted Enemy Units get +1 to the AP of their Weapon Attacks.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="AEF 21st Mobile Armor Division “Polar Bears”" id="14f9-fe25-0fba-bf96" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="3" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="error" type="add" value="This Specialization requires at least three Walker Units.">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="7da2-822e-291f-eccc" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" scope="parent" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="3"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="In the Shop" id="085f-80f6-02b5-a5e1" hidden="false" typeId="60a8-a233-a953-97f1" typeName="Special Requisition">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Cost" typeId="fdc2-ccd7-0950-5670">4 SP</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Effects" typeId="8280-2b12-dd95-5313">At the end of the round, after VP has been tallied, you may select one Engineer Unit in your Deployment Zone and take a destroyed non-Superheavy Walker or Battlesuit Unit from your army and redeploy it at half strength in base to base contact with that squad.


*If a multi-model is selected you receive half of the models back, rounded up. If a single model is selected it will be returned at half Health, rounded up. All Upgrades are still applied to the unit purchased, but if it had a unit mounted within, that is not included.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Full Sprint" id="1a10-cbf7-152b-1fab" hidden="false">
              <description>When this Unit performs a Move and Dash action in the same turn, Melee weapons it controls gain +2 to their A.P. profile.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Steel Legs" id="5f8b-667c-37f0-60a6" hidden="false">
              <description>Units in your Army with the Walker Sub-Type gain the following Special Rules: Full Sprint, Logging Company, One with the Forest</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="One with the Forest" id="263f-d741-aeed-c710" hidden="false">
              <description>When this Unit takes the Fallback Reaction it gains a level of Obscuring Until the end of the Attacking Player’s Activation.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Logging Company" id="2cd5-0413-5e71-ee6f" hidden="false">
              <description>This Unit gains the Demolish Action as a Standard Action.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="US Marines 7th Regiment “Magnificent Seventh”" id="93d3-06cb-f994-f20e" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="4" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Snake Eaters" id="80e1-8fef-6b92-3916" hidden="false">
              <description>Troop Units in this army gain the Amphibious Special Rule, and ignore Rough Terrain.

Troops Units in this Army gain 1 A.P. to their Attacks for each Level of Cover that applies to the Target.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Landing Party" id="37fe-9194-0e10-c657" hidden="false">
              <description>Units in this Army may not be placed En Route, and must be Deployed in the Setup Phase at the beginning of the Game. They may still be Embarked in Transports at the start of the game. 


M39 Buffalo Landing Vehicles in this army gain the Forward Deployment Special Rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="US Army 2nd Armored Division “Hell on Wheels”" id="97ce-df67-d92a-e88d" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="5" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="error" type="add" value="This Specialization requires either 2 Platoons that are either Mechanized or Armor">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="and">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="fae0-4a12-4ae4-5f9b" field="forces" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="29bb-b3e2-3fbb-9ad5" field="forces" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="fae0-4a12-4ae4-5f9b" field="forces" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="2"/>
                    <condition childId="29bb-b3e2-3fbb-9ad5" field="forces" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="2"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Hell on Wheels" id="4969-fd69-7901-8f54" hidden="false">
              <description>Vehicle units gain Capture as a Standard Action instead.


Tracked Vehicles gain an Aim Token if they Move a distance that is more than half of their Movement Statistic away from their starting position during their Activation.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Iron Guts" id="ca94-01f8-2da3-e3e7" hidden="false">
              <description>Units in this army may re-roll any failed dice once during Bailout rolls.


Troop Units that have Disembarked from a Transport this Round (except as a result of a Bailout), are treated for the rest of the round as having one Level of Cover.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="US Army 3rd Infantry Division Artillery “Marne Thunder”" id="a584-d769-ac55-0dde" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="6" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="error" type="add" value="This Specialization requires at least one Artillery Platoon">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="d61b-5a5c-9008-3c0b" field="forces" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Bombs Bursting In Air" id="e008-a178-b4ef-db82" hidden="false">
              <description>If an attack from an Ordnance X weapon in this army destroys at least 1 Unit that is within range of an Objective Marker, that Objective Marker becomes uncaptured.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Rocket’s Red Glare" id="9db4-b646-7ff4-13ce" hidden="false">
              <description>Increase the Hits profile of Ordnance X weapons by 1 when hitting an enemy Unit, and decrease the hits by 1 when hitting a friendly Unit, to a minimum of 1.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="AEF Cavalry 29th Concordian Regiment “Yellowjackets”" id="7b56-cd3e-ba27-84a9" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="7" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="error" type="add" value="This Specialization requires at least one Recon Platoon">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="df9c-5241-555f-2018" field="forces" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Hold Out For The Cavalry" id="b78c-31c5-06bb-3e76" hidden="false">
              <description>Before deployment, select 1 platoon in your army. That platoon is the only one that will be deployed during the first setup phase. No units in this platoon may be placed En Route for any reason. All other units in your army are En Route, using the Sound The Bugles rule for deployment in place of any other rule they may have for En Route deployment.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Circle The Wagons" id="ddb7-772a-d9ff-9707" hidden="false">
              <description>If a Friendly Unit is within 3&quot; of this Unit, this Unit improves their Cover by 1.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Sound The Bugles" id="44a5-e90d-4191-f319" hidden="false">
              <description>Each Setup Phase after the first battle round, for each undeployed platoon in your army, you may roll to Sound the Bugles and see if they arrive. Roll a die, and add 1 to the result for each completed Round. On a 7+, the Cavalry arrives! Choose any table edge, and deploy all models in this platoon within 8&quot; of that table edge and more than 8&quot; away from any enemy units. You may not Sound The Bugles if you have no units on the table. In the Round this Platoon arrives, all units in that Platoon benefit from the following bonuses:

* +1 to Hit for each round that has passed.
* +2&quot; to Movement for each round that has passed.
* Units in this Platoon are treated as benefiting from one additional piece of Obscuring Terrain for purposes of Ranged Attacks
* Units that enter Engagement with an Enemy Unit apply a Suppression Token to that Unit.
* Units in this Platoon may perform the Rally action as a Free Action.

In the fourth Round’s Setup Phase, if there are still platoons En Route, and all Sound the Bugles rolls are failed this Round, the units in those platoons must deploy within 8&quot; of the edge closest to your deployment zone, and gain no benefits from Sound the Bugles.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
